    },
    "ssky_text_block_VcMJLz": {
      "type": "ssky-text-block",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_6iyLCb": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<p>The Reality is Kids Need to Be Exposed to the Free Market and Taught How It Works</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "left",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_weight": "bold",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "center": false
          }
        },
        "text_TgJaKV": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 64,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "left",
            "text": "<p>A Lack of This Knowledge Inhibits Their Ability to Innovate, Negotiate, and Compete in the Real World.</p>",
            "text_size": "extra-large",
            "text_weight": "bold"
          }
        },
        "text_raD8d9": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 84,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "left",
            "text": "<p>There’s a problem, though. Most of us parents weren’t taught these ideas very well in school. As a result, you may feel inadequate in talking to your kids about economic ideas.</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular"
          }
        },
        "text_with_icon_tXMPWQ": {
          "type": "text_with_icon",
          "settings": {
            "alignment": "left",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/icon-five.svg",
            "text": "<p><strong>Are you concerned you don’t have the knowledge or confidence to teach your kids about ideas of the free market and how they relate to their life? </strong><br/>Hoping that, somehow, they will be curious enough to figure it out for themselves?</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "text_b": "",
            "custom_color_b": ""
          }
        },
        "text_with_icon_wbp4mF": {
          "type": "text_with_icon",
          "settings": {
            "alignment": "left",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/icon-six.svg",
            "text": "<p><strong>Do you want to find educational resources to teach your child sound economic principles, but don't know where to look?</strong>  It’s hard to know what's aligned with your values, and ideas, and even to know which messages you want to share with your family.</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "text_b": "",
            "custom_color_b": ""
          }
        },
        "text_with_icon_GfHJqq": {
          "type": "text_with_icon",
          "settings": {
            "alignment": "left",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/icon-seven.svg",
            "text": "<p><strong>Do you question whether your kids will be interested in (or even understand) these real-world concepts?</strong> Perhaps you barely understand them yourself, and you wonder how to help your children become well rounded in learning these ideas.</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "text_b": "",
            "custom_color_b": ""
          }
        },
        "text_kfeXjW": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 62,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "left",
            "text": "<p><br/>After all, you only have one shot at helping shape your children’s worldview before the noise of today’s society takes over.<br/><br/>Fortunately, you are not alone. And you can let go worrying that your children are not receiving the quality of education that they deserve.</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_6iyLCb",
        "text_TgJaKV",
        "text_raD8d9",
