    "ssky_text_block_APVcg6": {
      "type": "ssky-text-block",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_kYqRnd": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<p>More Than Anything… You Need a Helping <br/>Hand to Teach True Economic Principles to <br/>Your Children—A Curriculum Designed to <br/>Empower You and Your Kids</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "center",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_weight": "bold",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "center": false
          }
        },
        "text_nxbMcM": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 72,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "center",
            "text": "<p>But Right Now Trying to Teach Kids About Economics Seems Painful and Difficult for Everyone Involved…</p>",
            "text_size": "extra-extra-large",
            "text_weight": "medium"
          }
        },
        "text_88kqHC": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 120,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "center",
            "text": "<p>Learning about the free market isn’t always easy, though maybe this sounds familiar:</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "semibold"
          }
        },
        "text_with_icon_4KejYf": {
          "type": "text_with_icon",
          "settings": {
            "alignment": "left",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/icon-sad.webp",
            "text": "<p>A trip to the <strong>Local Library</strong> in search of good literature results in frustration that many books are pushing harmful agendas that are appealing to kids. You wonder what good material you can introduce to your children that they’ll actually enjoy.</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "icon_b": "shopify://shop_images/icon-sad.webp",
            "text_b": "<p>After finding <strong>YouTube Videos</strong> from creators that seemed good at the time for your kids, you discovered that they ultimately had some agenda and were using their platform to promote ideas you strongly disagree with.</p>",
            "custom_color_b": ""
          }
        },
        "text_with_icon_cH8aQj": {
          "type": "text_with_icon",
          "settings": {
            "alignment": "left",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/icon-sad.webp",
            "text": "<p>You have broached big subjects in <strong>Family Discussions</strong> after dinner that end up in silence from apathetic kids or end awkwardly when your kids ask questions you can’t answer.</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "icon_b": "shopify://shop_images/icon-sad.webp",
            "text_b": "<p>Perhaps you use <strong>Current Events</strong> to try and educate your child about economics but it’s too complex to explain. Often, you wonder if what you’re doing is enough to “stick” and prepare your children for the world they’re growing up in.</p>",
            "custom_color_b": ""
          }
        },
        "text_cGkQPz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 86,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "center",
            "text": "<p>Your kids are sometimes left with more questions than answers, and you can’t bear the thought of them getting lost at sea in all the socialist ideas being popularized today.<br/><br/>What if the solution to this problem was simpler than you thought?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "regular"
          }
        }
      },
